{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Codechef {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        sc.nextLine();\n        String input = sc.nextLine();\n        \n        int maxLength = 0;\n        int innerCount = 0;\n        int segmentStart = 0;\n        \n        int lastClose = input.lastIndexOf(')');\n        for (int i = 0; i < input.length(); i++) {\n            if (input.charAt(i) == '(') {\n                String segment = input.substring(segmentStart, i);\n                processSegment(segment, (len) -> {\n                    if (len > maxLength) maxLength = len;\n                });\n                \n                int closeIndex = input.indexOf(')', i);\n                if (closeIndex == -1) break;\n                \n                String inner = input.substring(i + 1, closeIndex);\n                processInner(inner, (token) -> {\n                    if (!token.isEmpty()) innerCount++;\n                });\n                \n                segmentStart = closeIndex + 1;\n                i = closeIndex;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        String finalSegment = input.substring(segmentStart);\n        processSegment(finalSegment, (len) -> {\n            if (len > maxLength) maxLength = len;\n        });\n        \n        System.out.println(maxLength + \" \" + innerCount);\n    }\n    \n    static void processSegment(String s, Consumer<Integer> consumer) {\n        for (String token : s.split(\"_\")) {\n            consumer.accept(token.length());\n        }\n    }\n    \n    static void processInner(String s, Consumer<String> consumer) {\n        for (String token : s.split(\"_\")) {\n            consumer.accept(token);\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <functional>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nvoid processSegment(const std::string& s, const std::function<void(int)>& consumer) {\n    std::vector<std::string> tokens;\n    size_t start = 0;\n    size_t end = s.find('_');\n    \n    while (end != std::string::npos) {\n        tokens.push_back(s.substr(start, end - start));\n        start = end + 1;\n        end = s.find('_', start);\n    }\n    tokens.push_back(s.substr(start));\n    \n    for (const auto& token : tokens) {\n        consumer(token.length());\n    }\n}\n\nvoid processInner(const std::string& s, const std::function<void(const std::string&)>& consumer) {\n    std::vector<std::string> tokens;\n    size_t start = 0;\n    size_t end = s.find('_');\n    \n    while (end != std::string::npos) {\n        tokens.push_back(s.substr(start, end - start));\n        start = end + 1;\n        end = s.find('_', start);\n    }\n    tokens.push_back(s.substr(start));\n    \n    for (const auto& token : tokens) {\n        consumer(token);\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    std::string line;\n    \n    // Skip first line\n    std::getline(std::cin, line);\n    \n    // Read input string\n    std::getline(std::cin, line);\n    \n    int maxLength = 0;\n    int innerCount = 0;\n    int segmentStart = 0;\n    \n    size_t lastClose = line.rfind(')');\n    \n    for (size_t i = 0; i < line.length(); i++) {\n        if (line[i] == '(') {\n            std::string segment = line.substr(segmentStart, i - segmentStart);\n            processSegment(segment, [&maxLength](int len) {\n                if (len > maxLength) maxLength = len;\n            });\n            \n            size_t closeIndex = line.find(')', i);\n            if (closeIndex == std::string::npos) break;\n            \n            std::string inner = line.substr(i + 1, closeIndex - i - 1);\n            processInner(inner, [&innerCount](const std::string& token) {\n                if (!token.empty()) innerCount++;\n            });\n            \n            segmentStart = closeIndex + 1;\n            i = closeIndex;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    std::string finalSegment = line.substr(segmentStart);\n    processSegment(finalSegment, [&maxLength](int len) {\n        if (len > maxLength) maxLength = len;\n    });\n    \n    std::cout << maxLength << \" \" << innerCount << std::endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00019393471302464604, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -7.819823804311454e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -0.011524885892868042, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.318679541349411, -0.00218593399040401, -5.483612312673358e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.3223240375518799, -0.07889118045568466, -0.0003413571394048631, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.32441219687461853, -0.10020949691534042, -0.011842658743262291, -3.6477376852417365e-05, -8.67805938469246e-05, -0.00012361239350866526, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -3.576278118089249